{%- comment -%}
  low-stock.liquid — real scarcity only (§9.2 rule 4, §9.1).

  Renders ONLY when the merchant actually tracks inventory for the variant
  and the remaining quantity is at or below their threshold. Untracked
  inventory returns nothing — not an empty wrapper, nothing — because a
  low-stock claim on untracked stock is a fabricated claim, and shipping the
  ability to make one hands the buyer's store a liability.

  `continue` selling past zero is also excluded: if the merchant is happy to
  oversell, the item is not scarce.

  Threshold is `settings.cro_low_stock_threshold`; 0 disables the feature.

  Params:
    variant  (variant, required)
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign threshold = settings.cro_low_stock_threshold | default: 0

  assign should_render = false
  if threshold > 0 and variant != blank and variant.available
    if variant.inventory_management != blank and variant.inventory_policy != 'continue'
      if variant.inventory_quantity > 0 and variant.inventory_quantity <= threshold
        assign should_render = true
      endif
    endif
  endif
-%}

{%- if should_render -%}
  <p class="low-stock" role="status">
    {%- render 'icon', icon: 'alert', size: 16 -%}
    <span>{{ 'products.product.low_stock' | t: count: variant.inventory_quantity }}</span>
  </p>
{%- endif -%}
